      {
        "id": 242594,
        "name": "Trajector",
        "username": "Trajector",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
        "created_at": "2022-02-10T15:33:38.284Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I’m kind of surprised Unity isn’t on that cover, honestly. And, hey, Christopher, you know very well that isn’t how “light year” works! <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/laughing.png?v=12\" title=\":laughing:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":laughing:\"></p>\n<p>I recall learning that kangaroos are better for the health of grasslands than cows, because they don’t rip out the grass by the roots and they don’t have hooves to trample the turf. Nor do they fart methane. And indeed, they <em>are</em> super delicious! So, c’mon, Australia, export some stock kangaroos all over the place! It’s for the good of the planet!!!</p>\n<p>Great episode. Really fun.</p>",
        "post_number": 23,
